1
00:00:00,330 --> 00:00:02,582
On October eighth, twenty twenty five,

2
00:00:02,602 --> 00:00:05,989
more than five hundred police officers raided a prison

3
00:00:06,009 --> 00:00:08,640
outside Guatemala City. They counted the prisoners.

4
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:10,533
Two hundred and fifty six.

5
00:00:10,553 --> 00:00:11,669
Everyone was there.

6
00:00:12,789 --> 00:00:15,860
Three days later, twenty of them were gone.

7
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:18,564
Not ordinary prisoners. Leaders of Barrio 18,

8
00:00:18,584 --> 00:00:22,041
a gang the United States had just declared a

9
00:00:22,061 --> 00:00:22,814
terrorist organization.

10
00:00:23,534 --> 00:00:24,848
There was no tunnel.

11
00:00:24,868 --> 00:00:26,850
No broken wall. According to prosecutors,

12
00:00:26,870 --> 00:00:29,519
they most likely walked out through the door.

13
00:00:30,239 --> 00:00:32,940
A year later, we know what happened to every

14
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:35,359
one of them. Ten are back behind bars.

15
00:00:35,379 --> 00:00:36,568
One was found dead.

16
00:00:36,588 --> 00:00:38,382
And nine are still out there.

17
00:00:38,402 --> 00:00:40,801
One by one, here is how it happened.

18
00:00:42,541 --> 00:00:43,916
Chapter 1. The gang.

19
00:00:46,016 --> 00:00:49,257
Barrio 18 was born on the streets of Los

20
00:00:49,277 --> 00:00:51,069
Angeles, in the nineteen sixties.

21
00:00:51,089 --> 00:00:53,243
Its name comes from Eighteenth Street.

22
00:00:53,263 --> 00:00:56,505
Decades later, deportations from the United States helped carry

23
00:00:56,525 --> 00:00:58,317
the gang to Central America.

24
00:00:59,037 --> 00:01:00,589
In the nineteen eighties,

25
00:01:00,609 --> 00:01:03,341
another gang formed in the same city,

26
00:01:03,361 --> 00:01:04,914
among young Salvadoran immigrants.

27
00:01:04,934 --> 00:01:06,487
Mara Salvatrucha. MS thirteen.

28
00:01:06,507 --> 00:01:08,452
The two became bitter enemies,

29
00:01:08,472 --> 00:01:11,991
and they took that war with them to Central

30
00:01:12,011 --> 00:01:12,384
America.

31
00:01:13,104 --> 00:01:16,669
In Guatemala, it grew into one of the two

32
00:01:16,689 --> 00:01:19,059
most powerful gangs in the country,

33
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:20,652
alongside its great rival,

34
00:01:20,672 --> 00:01:22,644
MS thirteen. Its main business,

35
00:01:22,664 --> 00:01:24,237
according to the authorities,

36
00:01:24,257 --> 00:01:25,830
is extortion. Bus drivers,

37
00:01:25,850 --> 00:01:27,424
shop owners, small businesses.

38
00:01:27,444 --> 00:01:29,017
Pay, or be killed.

39
00:01:29,737 --> 00:01:32,547
In Guatemala, bus drivers have been among the most

40
00:01:32,567 --> 00:01:33,804
frequent victims. For years,

41
00:01:33,824 --> 00:01:36,634
drivers who did not pay were shot at the

42
00:01:36,654 --> 00:01:37,892
wheel, in broad daylight.

43
00:01:38,612 --> 00:01:41,206
And like many gangs in the region,

44
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:43,820
Barrio 18 was largely run from prison.

45
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,688
Leaders gave orders by phone.

46
00:01:45,708 --> 00:01:47,182
In later prison searches,

47
00:01:47,202 --> 00:01:50,169
police reported finding a clandestine extortion call center.

48
00:01:50,889 --> 00:01:52,378
In twenty twenty five,

49
00:01:52,398 --> 00:01:55,018
the government tried to cut those lines.

50
00:01:55,038 --> 00:01:58,413
In August, it moved top gang leaders into isolation.

51
00:01:58,433 --> 00:02:01,807
Barrio 18 and MS thirteen answered with coordinated riots

52
00:02:01,827 --> 00:02:04,448
in two prisons. A guard was killed.

53
00:02:04,468 --> 00:02:05,956
Others were taken hostage.

54
00:02:06,676 --> 00:02:10,176
In September, the United States designated Barrio 18 as

55
00:02:10,196 --> 00:02:11,740
a foreign terrorist organization.

56
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:15,260
Guatemala was under pressure to show it could hold

57
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:16,433
the gang's leaders.

58
00:02:17,153 --> 00:02:19,966
Three weeks later, it lost twenty of them.

59
00:02:21,706 --> 00:02:23,382
Chapter 2. The count.

60
00:02:25,482 --> 00:02:28,944
Fraijanes Two is a men's detention center in Fraijanes,

61
00:02:28,964 --> 00:02:32,426
a town about twenty kilometers southeast of Guatemala City.

62
00:02:32,446 --> 00:02:35,908
It held some of the most dangerous members of

63
00:02:35,928 --> 00:02:39,002
Barrio 18. Around two hundred and fifty men.

64
00:02:39,722 --> 00:02:41,331
On Wednesday, October eighth,

65
00:02:41,351 --> 00:02:43,367
a judge authorized a search.

66
00:02:43,387 --> 00:02:46,218
Five hundred and forty nine police officers,

67
00:02:46,238 --> 00:02:49,882
forty nine prison guards and a team of anti

68
00:02:49,902 --> 00:02:51,511
extortion prosecutors went in.

69
00:02:52,231 --> 00:02:54,107
They were looking for phones,

70
00:02:54,127 --> 00:02:56,002
signal boosters and SIM cards.

71
00:02:56,022 --> 00:02:59,414
Prisoners were taken out into a yard and searched.

72
00:02:59,434 --> 00:03:02,825
Police seized more than fourteen thousand quetzales in cash.

73
00:03:03,545 --> 00:03:06,157
And the official record of that day says the

74
00:03:06,177 --> 00:03:08,496
total matched. Two hundred and fifty six prisoners.

75
00:03:09,216 --> 00:03:12,343
But according to a prosecutor who took part,

76
00:03:12,363 --> 00:03:15,883
nobody checked identities. Nobody asked for the list of

77
00:03:15,903 --> 00:03:17,456
names. They counted bodies,

78
00:03:17,476 --> 00:03:18,243
not faces.

79
00:03:18,963 --> 00:03:20,318
On Friday, October tenth,

80
00:03:20,338 --> 00:03:23,412
the prison system's intelligence unit warned its director that

81
00:03:23,432 --> 00:03:25,131
there might have been escapes.

82
00:03:25,851 --> 00:03:28,299
On Saturday, a new record was written.

83
00:03:28,319 --> 00:03:29,710
Twenty prisoners were missing.

84
00:03:31,030 --> 00:03:32,509
On Sunday, October twelfth,

85
00:03:32,529 --> 00:03:35,883
the director of the prison system went in front

86
00:03:35,903 --> 00:03:38,882
of the cameras. Twenty members of Barrio 18,

87
00:03:38,902 --> 00:03:41,507
he said, had evaded the security controls.

88
00:03:42,447 --> 00:03:44,541
Chapter 3. Through the door.

89
00:03:46,641 --> 00:03:48,427
The first question was obvious.

90
00:03:48,447 --> 00:03:51,678
How do twenty gang leaders disappear from a high

91
00:03:51,698 --> 00:03:53,484
security prison without anyone noticing?

92
00:03:54,204 --> 00:03:56,211
The director's own answer was striking.

93
00:03:56,231 --> 00:03:57,563
The escape, he said,

94
00:03:57,583 --> 00:03:59,590
may have been planned long before,

95
00:03:59,610 --> 00:04:01,618
with help from inside and outside.

96
00:04:01,638 --> 00:04:03,645
The men did not leave together.

97
00:04:03,665 --> 00:04:05,334
They left one by one,

98
00:04:05,354 --> 00:04:08,375
or in pairs, possibly over the previous two months.

99
00:04:09,095 --> 00:04:10,945
Prosecutors later narrowed it down.

100
00:04:10,965 --> 00:04:13,562
Based on video hearings and visitor logs,

101
00:04:13,582 --> 00:04:16,926
they said the escape most likely happened between October

102
00:04:16,946 --> 00:04:19,169
eighth and eleventh. In other words,

103
00:04:19,189 --> 00:04:20,665
possibly after that search,

104
00:04:20,685 --> 00:04:24,029
possibly while the official count still said everyone was

105
00:04:24,049 --> 00:04:24,403
there.

106
00:04:25,123 --> 00:04:27,389
Investigators found no tunnels and no damage.

107
00:04:27,409 --> 00:04:30,328
A prosecutor said the men most likely got out

108
00:04:30,348 --> 00:04:32,287
with the cooperation of prison staff.

109
00:04:32,307 --> 00:04:33,593
That is an allegation,

110
00:04:33,613 --> 00:04:36,205
and the case is still in the courts.

111
00:04:36,925 --> 00:04:40,159
Witnesses quoted by Guatemalan media described something else.

112
00:04:40,179 --> 00:04:43,820
Prison system trucks entering Fraijanes on three different days,

113
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:45,447
supposedly for medical transfers.

114
00:04:45,467 --> 00:04:49,108
Investigators said the prisoners left in at least three

115
00:04:49,128 --> 00:04:52,768
groups. These claims have not been proven in court.

116
00:04:53,488 --> 00:04:56,846
And the cameras? Prosecutors said the cameras inside had

117
00:04:56,866 --> 00:04:59,098
been manipulated. There were no recordings.

118
00:04:59,118 --> 00:05:00,974
Then another detail came out.

119
00:05:00,994 --> 00:05:04,352
The prison system had lost access to its cameras

120
00:05:04,372 --> 00:05:06,979
in twenty of its twenty three prisons,

121
00:05:06,999 --> 00:05:09,981
because of technical failures and an expired contract.

122
00:05:10,001 --> 00:05:11,482
Nobody had reported it.

123
00:05:12,422 --> 00:05:14,424
Chapter 4. The fallout.

124
00:05:16,524 --> 00:05:18,359
The reaction was immediate.

125
00:05:18,379 --> 00:05:22,535
The United States embassy called the escape utterly unacceptable,

126
00:05:22,555 --> 00:05:24,854
and urged Guatemala to recapture,

127
00:05:24,874 --> 00:05:26,246
quote, these terrorists.

128
00:05:26,966 --> 00:05:30,281
Within a day, the director of the prison system

129
00:05:30,301 --> 00:05:32,134
was out. Within four days,

130
00:05:32,154 --> 00:05:33,987
the interior minister, Francisco Jiménez,

131
00:05:34,007 --> 00:05:36,581
and two of his deputies had resigned.

132
00:05:36,601 --> 00:05:39,546
President Bernardo Arévalo called it a serious failure.

133
00:05:40,266 --> 00:05:41,630
On October twenty fifth,

134
00:05:41,650 --> 00:05:43,708
police arrested twenty three prison guards,

135
00:05:43,728 --> 00:05:46,823
accused of helping the escape and failing in their

136
00:05:46,843 --> 00:05:49,593
duties. More arrests followed in the weeks after.

137
00:05:50,313 --> 00:05:53,324
Prosecutors asked for arrest warrants for the former head

138
00:05:53,344 --> 00:05:54,671
of the prison system,

139
00:05:54,691 --> 00:05:56,692
the prison's warden and a deputy.

140
00:05:56,712 --> 00:05:58,712
And for the former minister himself.

141
00:05:58,732 --> 00:06:01,070
But by then, according to Prensa Libre,

142
00:06:01,090 --> 00:06:03,090
Jiménez had already crossed the border.

143
00:06:03,110 --> 00:06:04,774
As of a month later,

144
00:06:04,794 --> 00:06:07,131
the warrants against him were still pending.

145
00:06:07,851 --> 00:06:11,234
The government offered a reward of one hundred and

146
00:06:11,254 --> 00:06:13,880
fifty thousand quetzales, about twenty thousand dollars,

147
00:06:13,900 --> 00:06:16,527
for each fugitive. Interpol issued red notices,

148
00:06:16,547 --> 00:06:19,551
because investigators believed some might run to Mexico,

149
00:06:19,571 --> 00:06:22,954
Honduras or Nicaragua. And the FBI sent a task

150
00:06:22,974 --> 00:06:24,088
force to help.

151
00:06:24,808 --> 00:06:26,127
Arévalo posted a promise.

152
00:06:26,147 --> 00:06:27,465
We will not rest,

153
00:06:27,485 --> 00:06:29,473
he wrote, until we catch them.

154
00:06:29,493 --> 00:06:31,815
Their days on the street are numbered.

155
00:06:32,755 --> 00:06:34,513
Chapter 5. The twenty.

156
00:06:36,613 --> 00:06:37,927
So who were they?

157
00:06:37,947 --> 00:06:39,262
According to Guatemalan media,

158
00:06:39,282 --> 00:06:42,265
nine of the twenty were members of the Rueda,

159
00:06:42,285 --> 00:06:45,268
the circle of leaders that runs Barrio 18 in

160
00:06:45,288 --> 00:06:47,604
Guatemala. Nine more led their own cliques,

161
00:06:47,624 --> 00:06:49,606
the local cells of the gang.

162
00:06:49,626 --> 00:06:51,608
And two were described as hitmen.

163
00:06:52,328 --> 00:06:54,544
Rueda means wheel. According to investigators,

164
00:06:54,564 --> 00:06:57,898
it is the inner circle that decides how the

165
00:06:57,918 --> 00:07:00,506
gang is run, inside prison and out.

166
00:07:01,226 --> 00:07:02,589
One clique stood out.

167
00:07:02,609 --> 00:07:05,700
Six of the twenty came from the same cell,

168
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:07,083
called Solo para Locos.

169
00:07:07,103 --> 00:07:08,465
Only for the crazy.

170
00:07:09,185 --> 00:07:10,643
Their names are public.

171
00:07:10,663 --> 00:07:13,229
Their aliases sound almost like a joke.

172
00:07:13,249 --> 00:07:14,706
Black Demon. Cartoon. Ketchup.

173
00:07:14,726 --> 00:07:17,662
Little Men. Happy. But according to the authorities,

174
00:07:17,682 --> 00:07:20,986
these were some of the most dangerous men in

175
00:07:21,006 --> 00:07:21,725
the country.

176
00:07:22,445 --> 00:07:23,973
Now, let's go through them.

177
00:07:23,993 --> 00:07:26,758
One by one. In the order they were found.

178
00:07:27,478 --> 00:07:28,910
Keep an eye on the board.

179
00:07:28,930 --> 00:07:31,088
Not all of them make it to the end

180
00:07:31,108 --> 00:07:31,814
of this story.

181
00:07:32,934 --> 00:07:34,509
Number one. Black Demon.

182
00:07:34,529 --> 00:07:36,104
Byron Eduardo Fajardo Revolorio,

183
00:07:36,124 --> 00:07:39,692
forty years old, leader of a clique called Latin

184
00:07:39,712 --> 00:07:43,281
Family. He lasted barely a day after the escape

185
00:07:43,301 --> 00:07:45,275
was announced. On October thirteenth,

186
00:07:45,295 --> 00:07:47,667
police found him in Santa Rosa,

187
00:07:47,687 --> 00:07:49,262
southeast of the capital.

188
00:07:49,282 --> 00:07:52,054
Two people with him were arrested too.

189
00:07:52,774 --> 00:07:55,978
Numbers two and three came five days later.

190
00:07:55,998 --> 00:07:57,591
Liro Strong and Monstruo,

191
00:07:57,611 --> 00:07:59,203
also known as Espectro.

192
00:07:59,223 --> 00:08:02,428
Police ran fourteen raids in the western highlands,

193
00:08:02,448 --> 00:08:06,055
and found them together in a house in Huehuetenango.

194
00:08:06,075 --> 00:08:07,668
According to Prensa Libre,

195
00:08:07,688 --> 00:08:10,892
they had been planning to cross into Mexico.

196
00:08:11,612 --> 00:08:13,966
Arévalo celebrated on social media.

197
00:08:13,986 --> 00:08:15,390
Seventeen to go.

198
00:08:16,110 --> 00:08:18,522
Number four. Brown. Nicolás Xante Sis,

199
00:08:18,542 --> 00:08:21,358
leader of a clique called Vatos Locos.

200
00:08:21,378 --> 00:08:22,979
On October twenty first,

201
00:08:22,999 --> 00:08:26,221
he was stopped on a highway in Escuintla,

202
00:08:26,241 --> 00:08:27,842
near the Pacific coast.

203
00:08:27,862 --> 00:08:31,084
Three people traveling with him were also arrested.

204
00:08:31,804 --> 00:08:33,302
Four caught in nine days.

205
00:08:33,322 --> 00:08:35,729
It looked like the rest would follow quickly.

206
00:08:35,749 --> 00:08:36,640
They did not.

207
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:40,885
It took another month to find number five.

208
00:08:40,905 --> 00:08:42,726
Cartoon. Ever Jonathan Sinay Dionicio,

209
00:08:42,746 --> 00:08:44,567
a member of the Rueda.

210
00:08:44,587 --> 00:08:47,881
On November twentieth, he was captured in a village

211
00:08:47,901 --> 00:08:49,354
in San José Pinula,

212
00:08:49,374 --> 00:08:50,826
just outside the capital,

213
00:08:50,846 --> 00:08:54,140
in an operation the government said had international support.

214
00:08:54,860 --> 00:08:57,218
Number six came just before Christmas.

215
00:08:57,238 --> 00:08:58,803
On December twenty third,

216
00:08:58,823 --> 00:09:01,180
police caught Milton Noel Najarro García.

217
00:09:01,900 --> 00:09:03,778
And then, on January fourth,

218
00:09:03,798 --> 00:09:06,815
twenty twenty six, the seventh man was found.

219
00:09:06,835 --> 00:09:07,954
But not alive.

220
00:09:09,474 --> 00:09:11,040
Edwin Roberto González Ortega,

221
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:14,214
known as Psyco, a member of the Rueda,

222
00:09:14,234 --> 00:09:17,784
was found in a rural area in Villa Canales,

223
00:09:17,804 --> 00:09:19,371
south of the capital.

224
00:09:19,391 --> 00:09:21,751
He had been shot multiple times.

225
00:09:21,771 --> 00:09:25,321
Police called it a direct attack by unknown attackers.

226
00:09:25,341 --> 00:09:27,304
Who killed him, and why,

227
00:09:27,324 --> 00:09:29,288
has not been made public.

228
00:09:30,008 --> 00:09:33,095
On January thirteenth, police arrested the partner of one

229
00:09:33,115 --> 00:09:36,203
of the fugitives, a clique leader known as Smoking.

230
00:09:36,223 --> 00:09:37,929
He himself was still free.

231
00:09:37,949 --> 00:09:41,036
Remember that name. It would take police more than

232
00:09:41,056 --> 00:09:42,763
eight months to find him.

233
00:09:43,703 --> 00:09:45,844
Chapter 6. Hostages.

234
00:09:47,944 --> 00:09:50,031
Days later, the gang struck back.

235
00:09:50,051 --> 00:09:51,435
Not with an escape.

236
00:09:51,455 --> 00:09:52,489
With a takeover.

237
00:09:53,209 --> 00:09:56,730
On January seventeenth, the government moved to cut the

238
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:58,698
privileges of imprisoned gang leaders,

239
00:09:58,718 --> 00:10:01,452
including Aldo Duppie, known as El Lobo,

240
00:10:01,472 --> 00:10:04,207
the head of Barrio 18 in Guatemala.

241
00:10:04,927 --> 00:10:08,100
Within hours, prisoners rose up in three prisons.

242
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:10,495
They took forty six workers hostage.

243
00:10:10,515 --> 00:10:12,091
Most of them guards.

244
00:10:12,111 --> 00:10:13,688
One was a psychologist.

245
00:10:14,408 --> 00:10:16,530
The new interior minister refused to negotiate.

246
00:10:16,550 --> 00:10:18,979
I will not give in to this blackmail,

247
00:10:18,999 --> 00:10:19,591
he said.

248
00:10:20,311 --> 00:10:23,513
The next morning, police and soldiers stormed Renovación One,

249
00:10:23,533 --> 00:10:25,662
a maximum security prison in Escuintla.

250
00:10:25,682 --> 00:10:28,884
They retook it, and took El Lobo into custody.

251
00:10:28,904 --> 00:10:31,391
Photos showed him with a bloodied shoulder.

252
00:10:31,411 --> 00:10:33,539
By the end of the day,

253
00:10:33,559 --> 00:10:35,330
all the hostages were free.

254
00:10:36,050 --> 00:10:38,521
But outside, the gang was hunting police.

255
00:10:38,541 --> 00:10:41,012
In attacks in and around Guatemala City,

256
00:10:41,032 --> 00:10:43,503
at least seven police officers were killed.

257
00:10:43,523 --> 00:10:46,706
Later reports raised the number to as many as

258
00:10:46,726 --> 00:10:47,062
ten.

259
00:10:47,782 --> 00:10:50,955
President Arévalo declared a thirty day state of emergency,

260
00:10:50,975 --> 00:10:53,084
and three days of national mourning.

261
00:10:53,104 --> 00:10:55,212
The army went into the streets.

262
00:10:55,232 --> 00:10:56,632
According to Prensa Libre,

263
00:10:56,652 --> 00:10:59,825
about three thousand three hundred people were detained in

264
00:10:59,845 --> 00:11:01,244
less than a month.

265
00:11:02,184 --> 00:11:04,127
Chapter 7. The long hunt.

266
00:11:06,227 --> 00:11:07,809
Back to the twenty.

267
00:11:07,829 --> 00:11:10,212
Number eight. Carlos Agustín Reyes Popol,

268
00:11:10,232 --> 00:11:12,615
known as Yoker. On January thirtieth,

269
00:11:12,635 --> 00:11:15,418
he was captured in San Pedro Ayampuc,

270
